# Cooler LCD panel (HID 5131:2007).
#
# The file name matters. TAG+="uaccess" only marks the device; the ACL is
# granted by the uaccess builtin, which runs from RUN{builtin}+ in
# 73-seat-late.rules. A rule numbered above 73 still gets its tag applied, but
# the step that consumes the tag has already run, so no ACL is granted. This
# must therefore sort before 73 -- 70 keeps it after 50-udev-default.rules, so
# these MODE/GROUP values win over that file's defaults.
#
# GROUP= is a backup for sessions where uaccess cannot resolve a seat (for
# example a systemd user service running outside the seat context). "users" is
# common but not universal; install substitutes the invoking user's primary
# group, which is why it is spelled out here for hand-copied installs.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="5131", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2007", MODE="0660", GROUP="users", TAG+="uaccess"
